{title: Blood of the Mighty Men}
{subtitle: 2 Samuel 23:13–17}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 70}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Bb] | [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The Philistines held the gate strong
David [Eb]waited in the [F]cave deep [Bb]
Three chief men heard the longing [Gm]song
And [Eb]rose while the [F]harvest was ripe [Bb]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Pour it [Eb]out to the Lord a[Bb]bove
It is [Gm]blood of the men who [F]died
Do not [Eb]drink from this cup of [Gm]love
For their [Eb]lives are the [F]price [Bb]paid
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
They broke through the [Eb]enemy camp [Bb]
And [Eb]drew wa[F]ter from the [Bb]well
The risk was [Eb]great and the danger [Gm]damp
But they [Eb]carried it [F]back to [Bb]town
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Eb]Far be it [F]from me to [Gm]take
This [Eb]sacrifice [F]of their [Gm]blood
The [Eb]mighty men went [F]at the [Gm]risk
[Eb]And gave their [F]lives to [Bb]God
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Such were [Eb]the exploits of the [Bb]three
Re[Gm]fusing to drink the wa[F]ter
Honor the [Eb]risk of the men for [Gm]me
And [Eb]keep the [F]holy or[Bb]der
{end_of_verse}
